{
  "name": "AI appointment reminder calls with Ringee, Google Calendar and n8n",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## AI appointment reminder\nAn AI voice agent phones each person shortly before a meeting to **confirm they will attend**, then the meeting is colour-coded in Google Calendar.\n\n**Flow 1 (top)** finds meetings starting in about an hour and starts one call each.\n**Flow 2 (bottom)** waits for the call to end, reads the AI's result and updates the calendar.\n\nRingee only publishes a few outcomes as events, so this workflow reads the result with *Get Call Result* after the call ends. That is reliable for every outcome.\n\n[Ringee](https://ringee.io) · [Docs](https://docs.ringee.io)",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 470,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "6345dfb1-8531-53c5-baad-1963151c4442",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -260,
        -330
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Before you run this**\n1. In Ringee, create a **Custom Integration** (Integrations → Custom Integrations) and copy its **API key** and **Signing Secret**.\n2. In n8n, create a **Ringee API** credential with both.\n3. Pick your AI voice agent in the Ringee node.\n4. Activate the workflow, then paste the **Ringee Trigger's Production URL** into the integration's **Outbound URL** and tick *Call Completed* and *Call Failed*.\n\n**Calendar convention:** put the person's phone number in the event description, for example `Phone: +14155550123` and `Name: Ada Lovelace`. Use an agent of type **Reminders & Notifications**.",
        "height": 330,
        "width": 470,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "85b2a72c-3e2e-5788-bd2d-9d331cfa65d3",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -260,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**No double calls.** Each call uses the calendar event ID as its *Idempotency Key*, so even if two runs see the same meeting, Ringee places the call once.",
        "height": 140,
        "width": 330,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "e5b8f9b9-32bb-51fc-bb33-692eea142650",
      "name": "Safe to run often",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        260,
        -330
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Consent and calling hours**\nOnly call people who agreed to be called, and only at reasonable hours. Ringee blocks numbers on your Do-Not-Call list and respects your plan's limits, but you are responsible for the permission to call. Every phone number in this template is fictional.",
        "height": 190,
        "width": 360,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "011c2953-6451-5d44-8031-dc71273ad396",
      "name": "Consent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        610,
        -330
      ]
    },
